One accepted rule per specs tier, each targeting the playbook, renders as a single `## Rules`
section: the count sentence carrying the playbook-only conflict clause and the pointer to the
record, then one bullet per rule in core → global → project order. Each tier's ref form shows —
the core namespace from config, the explicit global namespace, the bare project ref — and each
link form: absolute for a core tier living outside the plugin root and for the global tier,
repo-relative for the project tier. The section takes the lessons position, between the preamble
and `## Playbook Steps`.

